    {
      "claim_id": "majority-ground",
      "proposition": "The majority applies Preiser's distinction between prison conditions and release from physical imprisonment: a claim that earned First Step Act credits require transfer from prison to community-based prerelease custody is cognizable under Section 2241, notwithstanding continuing Bureau of Prisons legal custody, because the requested change is analogous to release on parole."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "ground-breadth",
      "proposition": "The majority limits its holding to claims seeking accelerated transfer out of prison to First Step Act halfway-house or home confinement, leaving ordinary transfers between prisons or security classifications unresolved rather than adopting a general rule for every reduction in the restrictiveness of custody."
    }
  ],
